  "arrangerNotes": "Verified against Beethoven's theme as engraved in the Wikipedia LilyPond score, including the famous syncopation at the end of the bridge (low 5 is one beat, then the 3 enters a beat early and is held two beats). Low 5 (dot below) means minLayout 11 on both drums. Lyric line breaks follow the hymn text; the early 3 starts the 'Giver' line. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums).",
  "verified": true
